# PSR-3b — Family runners + workflow reuse (careful slice)

## Scope

| Work | In this wave | Deferred |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Accept R3 family-runner consolidation | Yes (no code merge) | Adapter deletion |
| Reconcile `CI_COMPOSITE_SETUP.md` with repo reality | Yes | — |
| Migrate `portal-control-guard.yml` → `setup-platform` | Yes | Bulk workflow migration |
| Touch required-check names / branch protection | **No** | Later approved wave |
| Migrate phase-0/1/booking gates | **No** | Required-check wave |

## Family runners (R3)

Public commands already share `scripts/guards/run-guard-family.mjs`:

`guard:marketing` · `guard:workspace` · `guard:field-exposure` · `guard:guest`

Leaf guards remain for path-gated CI. Control-pack adapters and
`control:authority` stay separate. **No runner refactor in PSR-3b.**

## CI composite pilot (R4)

```yaml
- uses: actions/checkout@v4
- uses: ./.github/actions/setup-platform
  with:
    engine-check-enabled: "false"
- run: pnpm run control:ci
```

`engine-check-enabled: "false"` is mandatory for parity: the pre-pilot workflow
did not run `check-node-engine.mjs`. Enabling it would silently strengthen CI.

Machine inventory:
[`psr-3b-ci-reuse-inventory.yaml`](./psr-3b-ci-reuse-inventory.yaml)

Authority doc:
[`CI_COMPOSITE_SETUP.md`](../../platform/CI_COMPOSITE_SETUP.md)

## Metrics

| Metric | Before | After |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Workflows on `setup-platform` | 5 | **6** |
| Direct full bootstrap stacks | 18 | **17** |
| `MAIN_BRANCH_REQUIRED_CHECKS` length | 5 | **5** (byte-stable) |

## Local smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-3b-ci-reuse-smoke.mjs
```

Does **not** claim hosted Actions cache/parity. Expansion beyond this pilot
needs external Actions-run evidence (R4).

## Exit gate

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Family runners still share one implementation | required |
| Portal pilot on composite with engine false | required |
| Required trio workflows untouched | required |
| Required-check registry unchanged | required |
| `verify:*` tiers unmerged | required |
